  "laws": {
    "header": "length>=20; WDBC; u64(wrapping_u32(rows*stride)) + u64(strings_length)+20 <= actual_file_length; field_count not enforced",
    "icon_duplicate": "last row wins, including ID zero and empty strings",
    "spell_duplicate": "last row wins with new 64-byte payload",
    "selected_duplicate": "first matching row only; empty/invalid UTF8 result skips this requested ID",
    "dispel": {
      "1": "Magic",
      "2": "Curse",
      "3": "Disease",
      "4": "Poison",
      "other": ""
    }
  },
  "limitations": [
    "The producer loops, reader, UTF8 validator, display-ID collector/flattening and deduplication execute as original PE instructions; allocation, memcpy, hashing, dictionary insertion and u32 sorting are explicit seams. Replacement branches are checked separately as original instructions.",
    "Ghidra raw slices use a generic GCC ABI and omit external code/data; original Win64 instructions govern arguments and fields.",
    "Direct E8 candidates do not enumerate all indirect/computed/global references.",
    "Open/header failures return missing metadata after cleanup; exact native initialization synchronization and retry timing, error formatting, MPQ contents and OS file callees remain unexecuted.",
    "Static source tracing is not compilation, runtime validation or original/rebuilt parity."
  ],
